# x509_web_language.py's offline half, frozen: tests/fixtures/x509_web.neo verifies chains
# shaped like today's HTTPS sites (P-384/P-256/RSA issuers, SHA-256/384/512, mixed RSA/EC, SHA-1 trust
# anchors, a cross-signed root) issued by OpenSSL at the time written into each input, and the TLS 1.3
# CertificateVerify helper with OpenSSL signatures; tests/fixtures/x509_bundle.neo parses them all (bundle.out
# was checked against openssl x509 -text). Mode 0 input: [u8 host length][host][u64 time][u8 chain count]
# [u8 root count] then [u24 length][DER] per certificate.
